    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Brendan Kearns, Hills Property, is pleased to present this traditional detached cottage situated at Straboy, Glenties, Co. Donegal.\r\n\r\nExtending to approximately 48 sq.m. (516 sq.ft.), this two-bedroom bungalow occupies a site of approximately 0.15 hectares (0.37 acres) and enjoys a peaceful rural setting just off the R250 Glenties to Fintown road."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "The accommodation comprises an open-plan kitchen/living area, two bedrooms and a bathroom. While the property would benefit from modernisation and upgrading, it offers an excellent opportunity for purchasers seeking a cottage with character and the potential to create a cosy permanent residence, holiday home or investment property."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Rooms",
        "SortOrder": 2,
        "Content": "Kitchen / Living Area - 6.6m x 3.8m \r\nOpen-plan living space incorporating the kitchen and sitting area.\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 - 3.5m x 3.8m \r\nSpacious double bedroom\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 - 2.6m x 2.5m \r\nSingle bedroom, nursery or home office.\r\n\r\nBathroom - 3.6m x 2.0m \r\nBathroom located off the kitchen/living area.\r\n\r\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Purchasers may be eligible to avail of financial assistance through the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant Scheme, together with a range of SEAI home energy upgrade grants, subject to the relevant terms, conditions and eligibility criteria. These schemes may assist with the cost of renovating and improving the energy efficiency of the property.\r\n\r\nThe property offers ample outdoor space together with a detached derelict outbuilding, which may provide further potential subject to any necessary planning permissions and consents. The site also offers scope for extension of the existing dwelling, should additional accommodation be required.\r\n\r\nThe property enjoys the tranquillity of the Donegal countryside while remaining conveniently located within easy reach of Glenties, Fintown, and the many scenic amenities that this beautiful region has to offer, including walking routes, fishing opportunities and the nearby Bluestack Mountains.\r\n\r\nThis is a rare opportunity to acquire a traditional Donegal cottage with plenty of potential in a sought-after rural location."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
        "SortOrder": 4,
        "Content": "BER: G"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Viewing Details",
        "SortOrder": 6,
        "Content": "Viewing by appointment only.  For all enquiries, please contact Brendan at Hills Property on 085 1773362."
      }
    ],
